A directive on the losing declaration of a redeclared struct field: go/types keeps the
first field's Defs entry but not the second's, so a directive on the second would vanish
without a check. Like the sibling scanners, the field scan fails loudly rather than
silently dropping a recognized directive. The source itself does not type-check (the
loader tolerates it); plumb still reports the directive it cannot wire.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidType
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type S struct {
	A int
	//plumb:build
	A int
}

//plumb:build
func Use(s S) int { return 0 }
